{"id":"scaffold","ord":"a1","title":"Scaffold","done":"2026-08-09T13:06:54-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #56 (squash ee09573).\n- flake + npins (kolu@4d8a668, nixpkgs), Bun, drishti-style workspace, bunfig.toml isolated linker\n- @kolu/* hydrate + check-kolu-deps scripts\n- justfile whose `check` recipe IS the CI DAG (`[metadata(\"ci\")]`, odu-only — the planned GHA wrapper was dropped mid-flight at the human's direction)\n- linux + darwin lanes, bun2nix from juspay/bun2nix#2\n- **Effect wired in from day one:** effect + @effect/platform-node at the kolu pin's exact version (4.0.0-beta.106) with single-copy overrides\n- packages/core shipped a real @kolu/surface + Effect Schema cell exercised by bun test\n- **Stale:** that package is gone as of see-outline (PR #58), which split it into format/store/surface/server/web","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"hm-module","ord":"a2","title":"Home Manager module #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-10T09:55:14-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #64 (squash ea85270), authored by Grok, reviewed by Claude.\n- **Fix:** review caught a clean-stop-lands-failed systemd bug (Effect exits 130 on interrupt; SuccessExitStatus now declares it clean)\n- **Fix:** review also caught a README snippet that did not evaluate\n- **From the racket audit (2026-08-09):** the racket flake shipped a home-manager module running serve as a systemd user service (Linux) / launchd agent (macOS) with dataDir/host/port options\n- Port it for `olai web`","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"logging","ord":"a3","title":"Proper logging #techdebt","done":"2026-08-10T14:55:28-04:00","desc":"Added 2026-08-10 after the chat-agent notice shipped as a bare console line ('no ACP agent configured … so chat is off').\n- **Fix:** log the way kolu does — Effect's structured logging throughout the server (levels, spans/annotations, one consistent format, quiet-by-default with a verbosity switch), replacing the ad-hoc options.log/console.log seam\n- Study kolu's logging setup at the pin and match its shape\n- **Folded in from the sloppiness audit (2026-08-10), same seam:**\n  - serve.ts's fault path calls process.exit(1) from a bare .catch, bypassing the scope finalizers the file itself documents as load-bearing (deliberately untested)\n  - listener.ts still renders a raw String(cause) one file from the Cause.pretty helper built to prevent it\n  - OLAI_ALLOWED_ORIGINS is read inline with no named constant and no docs mention, unlike OLAI_DIST_DIR's exemplary pattern","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"bun2nix-fork","ord":"a4","title":"Drop the bun2nix fork #techdebt #upstream","done":"2026-08-10T12:13:40-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #67 (squash 232e774).\n- Upstream nix-community/bun2nix 2.1.2 turned out consumable without flake-parts; the fork input is gone\n- bun.nix equivalence proven by the bun-nix-fresh lane; darwin fix gained; flake.nix header rewritten to tell the new truth\n- **Filed 2026-08-10, a phase-1 watch item never itemized:** the flake's ONE external input was juspay/bun2nix#2 (the rawflake shape), carried because upstream nix-community/bun2nix's nix layer was flake-parts-shaped and could not be consumed\n- Upstream has since shipped fixes the fork lagged (2.1.2 carried a darwin nixpkgs fix at last check)\n- Re-check upstream's shape; if consumable, re-point and delete the fork dependency — if not, PR upstream the rawflake shape and then re-point","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"serve-surface-app","ord":"a5","title":"Upstream: serveSurfaceApp #techdebt #upstream","done":"2026-08-10T16:49:24-04:00","desc":"SHIPPED 2026-08-10 as PR #78 — olai's half, and the debt is paid: pin past kolu #2137 AND #2144.\n- listener.ts shrank from 321 lines to one serveSurfaceApp call\n  - plus the two decisions the primitive leaves: whose port this is (the EADDRINUSE fallback), and what a listener event sounds like (SurfaceAppEvent mapped onto @olai/log: stale tab Info, refused cross-site origin Warn)\n- **Kept outside the primitive:** the frame cap, now `RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES` inside the primitive with no option to move it, so #71 cannot recur\n- **Moved the OTHER way:** the surface runtime's lifetime, into serve.ts, which built it\n- listener.test.ts retargeted off the number onto the sink (real sockets, asserting on what the logger heard)\n- **Pin fallout (bunfig-invariant, not feature):** @kolu/url-shape joins the hydrate list; ws moves to the root manifest and leaves @olai/server; check-kolu-deps.sh grew peerDependencies\n- architecture.md's 'Owed upstream' note now reads 'Paid upstream'\n- **Evidence:** shutdown.test.ts caught the primitive's teardown hanging under bun (server.close's callback registered while a socket was open — node never sees it); that diagnosis went into kolu #2144, and the fence passes against the primitive now\n\nDISPATCHED 2026-08-10 → Kolu terminal e500de76 (Claude/Opus).\n- **PARKED same day:** the primitive's teardown hangs under bun (server.close registered while a socket is open — caught by olai's SIGINT fence); fix folded into the human's in-flight kolu listener-migration PR (kolu #2144); a re-pin past that merge unblocks\n\n**Kolu side SHIPPED 2026-08-10** as kolu PR #2137 (merged by the human):\n- serveSurfaceApp in @kolu/surface-app owns origin gate → upgrade → stale-tab → heartbeat → serve\n- payload cap sourced from the framework constant (unspellable to undercut)\n- 15 e2e tests\n\n**OLAI'S PAYBACK, dispatchable now:**\n- bump the kolu pin past #2137 (just update-pins)\n- delete packages/server/src/listener.ts's hand-rolled sequence in favor of one serveSurfaceApp call\n- shrink/retarget listener.test.ts (the #71 cap test may be subsumed by the primitive's own)\n- update architecture.md's debt note, and done-mark this item\n\n**Original filing:** Pay back the debt architecture.md has carried since phase 2: packages/server/src/listener.ts hand-sequences origin gate → upgrade → stale-tab check → heartbeat → serve, copied from kolu's own surface-app example.\n- PR kolu a serveSurfaceApp primitive owning that sequence; at the next pin bump olai deletes its copy and calls one line\n- Kolu-side work, zero olai conflict\n- (Filed 2026-08-10 — the sloppiness audit flagged this as a prose-only 'for now' with no tracking id)","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"run-reload","ord":"a6","title":"`just run` auto-reloads on source change","done":"2026-08-11T10:45:01-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 on the human's ask. `just serve` watches; `just run` deliberately does not (its comment says so). Wanted: auto-reload on source change for `just run`, with the recipe comment updated to the new truth and the sigint behaviour unregressed. Review waived by the human; evidence is a transcript in the PR description.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"precompress-upstream","parent":"upstream-dist-socket","ord":"a0","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient should emit precompressed siblings #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:49:20-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 from PR #93's review (this debt had no tracked home; the convention is an #upstream node, not a PR-body note). One half of the parent's ONE dist socket.\n- **The fact:** @kolu/surface-app's freshStaticLayer already NEGOTIATES precompressed assets (.br then .zst then .gz under the immutable prefix; identity when missing; shell never compressed; compressed media refused)\n  - but buildSurfaceClient does not EMIT the sibling files, so every consumer re-derives the post-step; olai's is packages/web/src/precompress.ts (PR #93)\n- **The ask:** a precompress option (or always-on) on buildSurfaceClient, single-sourcing what its own static layer serves\n- **When it lands:** olai deletes precompress.ts","see":["load-perf"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"keysbus-upstream","ord":"a7","title":"Upstream: keysBus broadcasts the full key set per new key #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T19:42:25-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 from PR #95 (snapshot-scale); a fix, not a receptacle (both debates).\n- **Shipped as kolu #2166** (merged 2026-08-13): a same-tick bulk add of M keys now costs ONE keys frame and ONE readAll (was O(M·N) full-set rebroadcast per key), with same-tick membership bursts coalesced\n- pinned by tests that fail against pre-fix server.ts (expected 100 frames to be 1), and the six pre-existing membership-contract cases untouched\n- Grok-reviewed clean; complete two-platform durable CI pass\n- olai benefits on its next kolu pin bump (riding olai#150's repin)","see":["snapshot-scale","surface-mcp-viewing"],"changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"log-pretty","ord":"a8","title":"Pretty logs on a TTY, logfmt everywhere else","done":"2026-08-11T14:31:06-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 from the human's ask (\"improve logging for human-friendliness, retaining agent-friendly format\").\n- Today `@olai/log` emits Effect's logfmt through one logger (`Logger.consoleLogFmt` / `formatLogFmt`, packages/log/src/sinks.ts) on every destination — correct for machines, dense for a human at a terminal\n\n**The design:** split by DESTINATION, not format.\n- When stderr is a TTY: a pretty sink (Effect ships `Logger.consolePretty`: local time, coloured level, message first, key=values dimmed after)\n- When piped / under systemd / in tests: logfmt byte-identical to today — the `@olai/log` testlib decoder and any agent parsing depend on it, so the pretty sink may only exist where no machine reads\n- `OLAI_LOG=logfmt|pretty` forces either way\n- Zero change to `toStdout`/`toStderr` call sites: the TTY check lives inside the sink layer\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-11 in two parts:**\n- PR #97 (squash 87cf89f) landed the split; its review completed post-merge — a process misfire, recorded on the PR itself\n- PR #99 (squash, tip f4ccd3e) carried the findings:\n  - `prettyFor(stream)` reading colour at emit time\n  - Wiring tests for both sinks that mutation-testing proved discriminating (three rounds of \"helper tested, wiring not\" before the lock actually held)\n  - `NO_COLOR`\n  - Per-logger `LogToStderr` scoping\n  - `OLAI_LOG` pinned at every harness spawn site\n  - The knob documented in docs/architecture.md\n","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"splitting-upstream","parent":"upstream-dist-socket","ord":"a1","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient takes splitting?: boolean #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:49:22-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 by the orchestrator on the load-perf-p1 author's flag (an #upstream ask with no tracked home is debt-in-prose). One half of the parent's ONE dist socket.\n\n- **The ask:** buildSurfaceClient accepts `splitting?: boolean` (today hardcoded false in its Bun.build call), so the code-split of markdown/highlight off the critical path (PR #118) stops needing a second hand-rolled Bun.build + shell rewrite (packages/web/src/markdown.ts).\n- **When it lands:** olai deletes most of markdown.ts. Details in PR #118's body."}
{"id":"upstream-dist-socket","ord":"a9","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient completed as ONE dist socket #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:49:24-04:00","desc":"Ratified from the lowy-electricity debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-12.md entry 1; all three stances signed). Shipped as kolu PR #2159, squash-merged 2026-08-12, with drishti pair PR #138 green.\n\n- **The receptacle:** \"what a surface-app dist is.\" Both children landed TOGETHER as one socket — precompressed siblings (.br/.gz/.zst) and `splitting` opened, shell never compressed, sibling-skip/prune in.\n- **The proof on the far side:** drishti's repin alone turned its identity-only dist into one carrying every sibling (main-*.js 640,266 B → 173,165 B brotli) — no drishti source change, exactly the socket thesis.\n- **Review:** independent reviewer; one MUST-FIX (the named .zst test was vacuous — deleting the zstd table row left the suite green), fixed and sabotage-verified; review also flushed a real gap (the extra-asset fixture sat under the 1024 B threshold, so sibling growth was never exercised). ts-pattern dep refusal accepted (Record keyed by the union; keeps the pair PR a pure repin). A late ci::e2e-governance red was an allowlist row for httpDrive.testlib.ts (Effect run-edge scan), delta-verified governance-only.\n- **Follow-up flagged, not taken:** kolu's own vite.config.ts emits .br/.gz but no .zst while its server prefers zstd — tracked in the PR body.\n- **Olai's side is NOT this item:** on the kolu pin bump, olai deletes precompress.ts and markdown.ts — the deletion is the installation. Stays in olai forever: Solid transform, Tailwind, fonts, icons.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"upstream-readout","ord":"aA","title":"Upstream: the connectSurface readout that cannot lie #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:50:37-04:00","desc":"Ratified from the lowy-electricity debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-12.md entry 2). Shipped as kolu PR #2160, squash-merged 2026-08-12, with drishti pair PR #139 green (Linux-only per the macOS rule; drishti has no branch protection at all).\n\n- **The defect paid for:** `connectSurface(...).status` could say `live` while a subscription over the socket had errored — olai shipped the bug this permits (a dead documents.keys rendering as an empty directory under a green light).\n- **The payment:** the conjunction folded into the readout (degraded state naming the stopped subscriptions); `pending does not degrade` as the universal default; `needsReload` travels. Event-folded, not walk-per-read.\n- **The cut held:** kolu owns the five states' TRUTH; the app keeps its LOOK. Notable deviation, reviewer-adjudicated sound: kolu's own client deliberately ignores conn.health (per-member onError policy, documented in wire.ts), so the in-repo proof is the surface-app example rail + seam tests, not a HostStatusPip migration.\n- **Review:** no code MUST-FIX; the vacuous dispose test was required fixed anyway (one standard across the batch) and sabotage-verified; two lying doc lines corrected; sibling-prefix readout assertion added. The rail-needsReload suggestion was declined as unreachable dead-path UI (its wire passes retired: reloadForUpdate).\n- **Olai's migration rides the later pin bump, not this item:** connection/status.ts shrinks to chrome (\"the files on disk reach this page\" stays this house's sentence).","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"upstream-chunking","ord":"aB","title":"Upstream: frame-limit chunking beside RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:25:21-04:00","desc":"Ratified from the lowy-electricity debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-12.md entry 3). Shipped as kolu PR #2158, squash-merged 2026-08-12.\n\n- **Why:** an oversized frame is not a failed call — the ndjson decoder closes the socket (1009) and takes every subscription on that tab with it. Every surface-app that uploads must chunk, and the arithmetic has been derived twice in kolu's orbit: padi's upload.ts, then olai's surface/src/attach.ts, which copied it \"because re-deriving it is how the same incident happens twice.\"\n- **The payment:** `chunkBase64` + the envelope/budget helpers landed beside RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES (the cap's own home). The arithmetic: base64 4/3, JSON envelope, no third expansion, chunk size a multiple of 3 so every 4-character group decodes alone. padi's upload.ts migrated in the same PR — the first copy is gone.\n- **The seam held (grok's cut, all three signed):** content policy stayed in olai — attachmentRejection, the allowlists, MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES, the tmp-directory rule.\n- **Review:** independent reviewer, one MUST-FIX — `frameBytesFor` was never exercised, so sabotage there left all 56 properties green; fixed and sabotage-verified both ways. The review also caught the old 26 MB fixture's expected value was not legal base64 (misplaced ceil). Drishti pair adjudicated unnecessary: purely additive export. CI: 48/48 required contexts green, both platforms.\n- **Still owed here:** olai's attach.ts shrinks onto the shared helpers on the next kolu pin bump — a separate beat.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-pin-sockets","ord":"aC","title":"Install the three sockets: kolu pin bump — the deletion is the installation #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T21:28:58-04:00","desc":"The olai-side halves of the three lowy-electricity payments, all on ONE pin bump. Shipped as PR #129 (d5b302c), squash-merged 2026-08-13. 30 files, net −563.\n\n- **Dist socket in:** precompress.ts and markdown.ts DELETED; build.ts composes buildSurfaceClient's own precompress + splitting; .zst finally emitted (br 189kB / zstd 199kB / gzip 225kB for the 700kB entry); the markdown chunk is one literal import() and first paint still never fetches it.\n- **Readout in:** status.ts shrank to the LOOK; the client.health() walk, unhealthy, readoutOf, needsReload all left; olai reads conn.readout itself (kolu's client deliberately doesn't auto-adopt).\n- **Chunking in:** attach.ts's derived-constants header replaced by kolu's frame-chunking helpers, imported at call sites; the content gate stayed whole.\n- **Review:** one MUST-FIX (the orchestrator's — a roadmap node naming the deleted file; resolved in this beat) + three NICE-TO-HAVEs taken, DELTA-OK; both sabotage hunts red. Beyond-brief: encoding.test.ts now drives every row of kolu's PRECOMPRESSED_ENCODINGS, .zst-arm sabotage-checked.\n- **Flags filed as nodes:** modulepreload-upstream (the 1.5kB unpreloaded shared chunk). The pipeline-<hash>.js naming right (was markdown-[hash].js) is pinned loudly by e2e.\n- **CI:** nine Linux contexts green at final head, GitHub CLEAN; macOS skipped per standing rule.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"modulepreload-upstream","ord":"aD","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient emits modulepreload for the entry's static chunks #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T11:25:26-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as kolu PR #2163** (squash e7f0391, admin-merged past the darwin gate on the human's approval 2026-08-13).\n- buildSurfaceClient walks the Bun metafile's import-statement edges transitively and splices modulepreload links into the shell; dynamic edges never followed; no-split entry byte-identical\n- Measured on Slow 3G: JS critical path 6110 ms → 4095 ms\n- Grok review APPROVE; all three NICE-TO-HAVEs taken\n\n- **olai collected it: PR #139 (squash d7cf177)** — the built shell now carries the modulepreload for the entry's shared chunk, verified in dist before merge. The loop #129 opened is closed.\n- **drishti pair: PR #140 (srid/drishti, squash dfcb26e)** — same repin, 12/12 CI green on the re-run (first run's typecheck miss was a workspace hydration hiccup: @kolu/solid-pwa-install invisible on the box, clean locally and on re-run).\n\nAll three repos now on kolu e7f0391.\n","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"owed-moves","ord":"aE","title":"Owed moves: GitState home, scale.ts home, wire.ts plugs into surfaceWsUrl #techdebt","done":"2026-08-13T14:33:36-04:00","desc":"Three small debts ratified by the 2026-08-13 lowy-electricity debate (items 3, 5, 6). **Shipped as PR #143 (squash 9bd7048), 2026-08-13.**\n- **(1) GitState** declared once in `format/src/committing.ts` beside RepoState.\n  - The reviewer diffed the deleted mirrors field-by-field against the new declaration.\n  - Surface re-exports, zero consumer churn; GIT_OFF traveled.\n  - ops' zero-importer public export (verified zero ON MASTER) dropped.\n- **(2) scale.ts → theme/** with every path reference followed (build, CSS banner, tests, fixtures, README).\n- **(3) wire.ts:36-39 deleted** — the dial calls the pin's `surfaceWsUrl(location.origin)` as a thunk.\n  - Laziness verified (import reads no location; URL parity checked across real origins).\n- **Claim tests:** `/connectSurface\\s*\\(/` equality with `[\"wire.ts\"]` (vacuity-probed both directions), and no client file outside `connection/status.ts` spells the readout's raw states.\n- **Pipeline:**\n  - Grok review — zero MUST-FIX, the zero-behavior-change claim held.\n  - NTHs taken (three READMEs follow the restory; regex widened). DELTA-OK twice.\n  - Then #141 and #142 landed: master merged (one real conflict in `chat/Entry.tsx`, both sides preserved; claims sweep extended over #141's new files).\n  - CI 10/10 at dba732a on kolu-ci-1.\n  - The author also caught and discarded a phantom-green first CI attempt (stream events with no durable artifacts) — re-ran and verified against per-node logs.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"fault-root-upstream","ord":"aF","title":"Upstream: a throw must not be a white tab — kolu takes a required `fault` #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T16:36:24-04:00","desc":"Debate-ratified 2026-08-13 (item 4; human approved every PR). **Fully shipped, both sides.**\n- **kolu #2164:**\n  - Composition root takes required `fault` like `retired`.\n  - `thrownText` printer upstreamed with the review-hardened lost-message rule (`firstLine === named` — the Grok review caught `includes` dropping short messages behind Safari frames, fixed red-first).\n  - The boundary records to console before the LOOK.\n- **kolu #2165:** `connectSurface.url` optional, defaulting via `surfaceWsUrl`, named error before allocation without a `location` (a fix, per Position C).\n- drishti paired at the master repin.\n- **olai #145 (squash 120904b):** kolu pin → dad81604.\n  - `main.tsx`'s hand ErrorBoundary + record + `thrown.ts` all deleted — the shell rides the standalone `SurfaceFaultBoundary` with `fault={(text) => <Fault text={text}/>}`.\n  - `Fault.tsx` keeps only the LOOK (pixel-identical, verified chalk+pitch with a real injected fault in the packaged binary).\n  - `wire.ts` drops its `url` line for #2165's default.\n  - Riders: `undoing.ts` takes Apply as an argument; bun-test gets a stub location.\n  - Missing `fault` is a compile error (sabotage: TS2322).\n  - The white-tab e2e now pins the heading olai owns and names its failure instead of a bare timeout.\n- **Pipeline:**\n  - Grok review (one MUST-FIX: README described the deleted wiring; three NTHs all taken).\n  - Delta-verify caught one more stale comment.\n  - Final sweep verified zero present-tense mentions of the old seam.\n  - CI green at 030b85b on kolu-ci-1.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"store-graduation","ord":"aG","title":"Leave @olai/store alone until it has proven stable — then decide whether it moves out","desc":"A watch item, not work.\n- The 2026-08-13 design debate noticed `@olai/store`'s source did not change at all during the busiest thirteen-PR week, suggesting it is finished enough to one day live outside this repo.\n- No move now.\n- **Open:** the trigger for revisiting.\n  - Two of the debaters said \"untouched across two consecutive releases, or 180 days without edits from 2026-08-12\" is enough.\n  - The third wanted 90 quiet days AND a second consumer of `Store.make`.\n- The human has not picked a wording.\n- When the trigger fires, decide then whether the package graduates.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00","custom":{"clock":"interrupted — debate #3 (2026-08-19) verified 8 commits into store/src since 08-13, the face (index.ts) twice; stillness counts from the LAST src edit, not 2026-08-12; and whether the socket absorbing volatility resets or reinforces the clock is the same wording question this node parks (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md, corrections)"}}
{"id":"agent-model-pin","ord":"aH","title":"Each repo pins its agents' model #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"Root cause 2026-08-13: every dispatched lane ran bare `claude`, whose machine default was Fable — burning the human's Fable limit all day.\n- Nothing pinned the model and Claude Code's footer never shows it.\n- **What was proven** (scratch-repo tests, valid):\n  - A repo `.claude/settings.json` with `\"model\"` + `\"permissions\": {\"defaultMode\": \"bypassPermissions\"}` makes a bare `claude` boot the pinned model with bypass on.\n  - The repo file beats the machine default.\n- **What was wrongly shipped and REVERTED:**\n  - The orchestrator hand-committed that file to olai and drishti WITHOUT authorization.\n  - `.claude/settings.json` is apm-generated output; hand-writing a generated surface was wrong twice over.\n  - olai: file removed (this commit); drishti: reverted (e987edc).\n- **The real fix must be apm-based** (the human's direction): these repos will adopt apm.\n  - The model/permissions pin gets AUTHORED in apm's source of truth and COMPILED into `.claude/settings.json`.\n  - Solution being designed — see apm-adoption.\n- **Interim, in force now:**\n  - Every spawn passes `--model opus --dangerously-skip-permissions` explicitly.\n  - The orchestrator verifies via /status before chartering.\n  - The machine default is also saved as Opus.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"apm-adoption","ord":"aI","title":"Adopt apm so agent briefs, skills and settings become versioned packages instead of per-lane rewrites #needs-brainstorm","desc":"Raised by the human 2026-08-13 while fixing the model-pin failure.\n- apm (Agent Package Manager) is a dependency manager for agent CONFIGURATION — skills, `.agent.md` definitions, prompts, MCP wiring — declared in `apm.yml`, compiled per-runtime.\n  - odu already ships its CI skill via `.apm/skills/`.\n  - drishti already carries `.claude/apm-hooks.json`.\n- **The prospect:** the orchestrator's hand-written per-lane BRIEF.md files, the Grok reviewer checklist, and the sabotage-verify discipline become versioned `.apm` packages.\n  - Portable across the claude/grok/opencode cast and installable into kolu/drishti instead of re-spelled per lane.\n- **Caveats found in its tracker:**\n  - Claude Code is a first-class deploy TARGET (settings.json, hooks, skills, marketplace) but not a runtime apm can launch.\n  - Grok target support merged experimental (#2420).\n- **Watch item:** if apm gains Claude Code as a launchable runtime with model config, it could absorb the launch layer that `.claude/settings.json` (see agent-model-pin) covers today.\n- Awaits the human's word on a design pass.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"orchestrator-home","ord":"aJ","title":"The orchestrator gets a real home inside olai — formalize what the prototype proved #needs-brainstorm","desc":"Opened 2026-08-13 after the Fable-limit burn and the compaction-memory problem.\n- Brainstorm at `docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md`.\n- **UPDATE 2026-08-16** — much of this is no longer hypothetical.\n  - Since 08-15 the orchestration runs as a live prototype in `docs/orchestrator/`.\n    - `agents.olai` (who can be hired and how).\n    - `dag.olai` (the pipeline template a PR walks).\n    - `lanes.olai` (the live board, one lane per PR, every step a node with after-edges).\n  - All written only through olai's own ops, with a terminal orchestrator driving kolu terminals and the human ruling at #human gates.\n  - Ten-plus PRs have shipped through it.\n- **What this item still owes:** turning that proven shape into olai proper — agents as nodes, lanes as nodes, approvals as verbs, launch via kolu — instead of a charter file plus one long-running chat.\n- **Open questions from the brainstorm:**\n  - Where the launch layer lives (command-in-node vs kolu structured spec vs apm as launcher).\n  - What of the prototype's conventions become product.\n- Awaits the human's picks.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"e2e-parallel","ord":"aK","title":"The e2e suite runs parallel by default, sized to the machine #techdebt","done":"2026-08-13T20:56:00-04:00","desc":"The human's dispatch, 2026-08-13, from the observation that the ~400-scenario suite ran serial everywhere. **Shipped as PR #153 (squash 823a679f), merged 2026-08-14 on the human's direct order.**\n- \"Just squash merge\" — review and remote CI skipped; the kolu-ci network was down and the change is test-infra.\n- Authored by GROK: parallel by default sized to CPU cores, `CUCUMBER_PARALLEL` stays the override (=1 serial).\n- All active lanes were told to merge master so their local CI e2e legs speed up immediately.\n- **Residual to watch:** the write-path 15s-wait scenario family that flaked under box load today.\n  - If parallelism surfaces it in normal runs, deflaking at the root becomes its own item.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"fonts-in-store","ord":"aL","title":"Fonts convert once, in the Nix store — not on every build #techdebt","done":"2026-08-13T23:03:47-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-14 on the human's report.\n- PR #152 had put the seam in the wrong place: `nix/fonts.nix` copied raw TTFs and `build.ts` converted all faces to woff2 on every client build.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-13** (night slate; the human pre-approved the merge): PR #155, squashed at master 9f1e1761.\n  - `woff2_compress` now runs in `@olai/fonts`' package-local `default.nix` (store outputs .woff2 directly, 70 faces).\n  - The client build only copies by name.\n  - `@olai/fonts` owns the catalog (`typefaces.ts`), the sheet (`css.ts`), `hosted.json` and the derivation; `nix/fonts.nix` deleted.\n- **Grok review:** 0 blocking, 1 nit (~40→70 docs figure, fixed in 5f113a3).\n- **Evidence** verified independently by the reviewer: store-vs-dist hashes identical, an independent reconversion byte-identical, a clean `just build-client` runs 0 conversions.\n- CI: 9/9 required Linux checks green at 5f113a3.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"child-receptacle","ord":"aM","title":"One shared owner for subprocesses (@olai/child) #human","todo":true,"desc":"The 2026-08-14 debate's ratified yield (three debaters, all-three signatures; the precise ledger is local at `debates/lowy-electricity-2026-08-14/conclusion.md` — the docs/ write-up was deleted at the human's word).\n- AWAITS THE HUMAN'S RATIFICATION before dispatch.\n- **The bundle:**\n  1. **A workspace leaf `@olai/child`** owning the subprocess plumbing spelled three times (`chat/pipes.ts`, `@kolu/detect`'s private copy, `recall/embedder.ts`).\n     - Owns: spawn, the exec-error race as typed `unstartable`, drained stderr with the caller naming the sink, kill-with-scope (SIGTERM → grace → SIGKILL).\n     - Explicitly OUT (unanimous): readiness, transport, restart policy, death-LOOK.\n     - Three deletions ride it: `embedder.ts:509`'s swallowed exec error (a bad `OLAI_EMBED_SERVER` should name the file, not time out on /health); `agent.ts`'s graceless bare `kill()` on clean stop; `pipes.ts`'s stale two-callers claim → claim test.\n  2. **Sidecar build unification**: `scripts/embedder.sh` is `scripts/acp-agent.sh` re-typed (its own comment confesses); one nix helper + one `scripts/sidecar.sh` replace both.\n     - The human's stronger shape from review: `nix/sidecars/<name>/default.nix` per sidecar (fonts spirit), the script shrinking to one generic lazy-loader for the dev loop only — the packaged binary is already fully baked.\n  3. **Two fences**: only recall/ reads the embedder env vars (gripping the read, scoped to packages/); only recall/ spells the cache path/tmp-rename.\n  4. **The kill-9 experiment** (decides whether the orphan sweep joins the leaf): nix-built serve, chat panel open, `kill -9` the olai pid, check ps for the adapter.\n     - Dies → sweep stays llama-own as ratified.\n     - Survives → sweep is shared and a 589 MB orphan is the strongest argument.\n  5. **detect's private unstartable**: ruled leftover-of-a-paid-socket; disposition open (export from `@kolu/detect` / wait for the leaf / leave 15 lines). Nothing filed upstream without the human.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"four-way-site-spelling","ord":"aN","title":"\"A place in the loaded set\" is spelled four ways in @olai/format #techdebt","done":"2026-08-15T17:30:07-04:00","desc":"Found during PR #170's refactor round (2026-08-14), both reviewers concurring: `{file, line}` spelled four ways in `@olai/format`.\n- **FIELDED FOR THE HUMAN 2026-08-15:** PR #188 at 5f92af7e, CI 9/9 green — and the four turned out to be SIX (the PR found `validate.ts`'s inline return type and a web component literally named Site hand-rolling the pair).\n- One `Site` in `node.ts` now.\n- **Drift property** proven both halves: a field added reddens all seven packages and lands on every carrier at once; before, it named only one of four.\n- Public surface 150→151 with Site deliberately reachable; behavior byte-identical, verified by printing export keys.\n- **Reviews:** Grok + opencode, zero blocking, no seventh spelling found by either.\n  - Two doc nits taken (the index header now carries no number beside an appendable list — it was wrong once before, #170's \"Eight\" — and confesses why).\n- **Declined on the record**, reviewers endorsing: no `Order.Order<Site>` for one-and-a-half consumers of different shapes.\n- Merge is the human's word.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:36-04:00"}
{"id":"read-request-inference","ord":"aO","title":"Read tools: TypeScript cannot infer their argument types, so every one spells them by hand #techdebt","done":"2026-08-17T22:27:25-04:00","desc":"Pre-existing, surfaced during PR #170 (2026-08-14): at ops/tools.ts:188 the request half's union Schema.Codec&lt;A,never,never,never&gt; | Schema.Top defeats inference of A, so every read tool hand-annotates its args. The answer half infers since #170. Either a tighter union or a second signature; small type-level work, no runtime change.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"230"}}
{"id":"outlines-quadratic","ord":"aP","title":"outlines() walks O(files × nodes), three passes per file #techdebt","done":"2026-08-15T21:57:00-04:00","desc":"Pre-existing, surfaced during PR #170 (2026-08-14): ops/query.ts:333's outlines() is O(files × nodes) with three passes per file. Untouched by #170 (out of its scope, both reviewers concurred). Matters as vaults grow; one pass with per-file accumulation is the obvious shape, measured before/after when taken.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"198"}}
{"id":"bun-watcher-bump","ord":"aQ","title":"File-watching costs one fd per file — bun 1.3.14 fixes it #human","todo":true,"desc":"The watcher-fd-cost investigation's ask (2026-08-14 night slate; full pricing in `docs/brainstorming/watcher-fd-cost.md`).\n- The one-fd-per-file cost is bun 1.3.13's watcher, O(every file under the root) — .git and node_modules included (2055 fds on a git-shaped corpus, 1004 of them on files olai never reads).\n- Bun 1.3.14's rewrite (Linux/macOS/FreeBSD together) is per-directory: 1050 → 15 fds, and it also closes the post-boot-subdir blind spot (see watcher-postboot-blind).\n- **Nine mutation shapes verified across the bump:** 1.3.14 delivers all nine, 1.3.13 seven.\n  - The one disagreement (create-by-rename source-vs-destination naming) costs olai nothing since `disk.ts:80-85` drops the payload at the edge.\n- `bun test` 1597/1597 on both binaries.\n- **Options, priced:**\n  1. Wait for nixpkgs — zero risk, unknown date, keeps cost + blind spot ← investigator's recommendation.\n  2. Bun override now — buys the fix, forks the runtime, darwin hashes on faith.\n  3. Hand-rolled per-directory watcher — halves the git case, still O(corpus), obsolete on the next bump, not recommended (and kqueue on Darwin makes it lossy).\n  4. Polling — forbidden by the ruling (changes latency/granularity).\n- The surface-mcp bridge is orthogonal: collapsing two stores halves the count but halving O(corpus) is still O(corpus).","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00"}
{"id":"olai-extension","ord":"aR","title":"Outlines are .olai files: the .jsonl extension retires","done":"2026-08-15T11:35:30-04:00","desc":"Ratified 2026-08-15 (docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md Question 3): PURE RENAME, hard cutover, manual mv; this repo migrates in the same PR.\n\n**Now** (2026-08-15):\n- Kolu terminal: `939eb88c` (Claude Opus, YOLO), branch `olai-extension`, PR #177.\n- **Delivered:**\n  - docs/roadmap.olai + docs/Archive.olai via git mv (byte-identical).\n  - OUTLINE_EXT carries the rule (code that decides reads it, prose that describes spells it out — a two-reviewer argument settled on the record).\n  - THE FENCE: tests/extension.test.ts sweeps every git ls-files path for .jsonl, string and filename, six named exemptions, all sabotage-proven.\n    - Its own review round caught the sweep reading packages/ only and choking on gitignored screenshots (git ls-files fixed both).\n- **Stage:** #review — Grok (`5f4fbcb7`) and opencode (`990a07e9`), briefed to hunt spellings outside the fence's reach and to verify the e2e suite actually exercises .olai fixtures (the silent-no-op failure mode).\n- **Parallel-lane fact:** if #175 lands first, this branch re-runs post-rebase and the fence catches #175's .jsonl spellings — the fence working as designed.\n- **Merge:** AUTONOMOUS once review clean + CI green (the human's ruling).\n  - OPERATIONAL NOTE at merge: every running olai server — the orchestrator's own ledger MCP included — reads .jsonl until restarted; the ledger goes quiet between merge and restart, and the human's other vaults migrate by hand (README carries the mv).\n- **Deferrals filed:** stem-strippers-twins, tree-sweep-fixture (which also carries the RCA-path human call).","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00"}
{"id":"stem-strippers-twins","ord":"aS","title":"Two functions strip an outline filename's extension with opposite rules — unify them #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:22-04:00","desc":"Found by PR #177 (2026-08-15), pre-existing: message.ts:148 and dates.ts:387 both strip an outline's suffix, with opposite stated arguments (spell the suffix vs find it). Unifying them needs its own argument. Related micro-fact from the same sweep: node.ts:253's isArchived allocates a string per call on a per-file-per-probe path.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"177","pr":"227"}}
{"id":"tree-sweep-fixture","ord":"aT","title":"Three tests each walk the whole repo tree their own way — share one walker when a fourth appears #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:24-04:00","desc":"Counted by PR #177 (2026-08-15).\n\n- acp/manifest.test.ts:76, the claims sweeps, and now tests/extension.test.ts each walk the whole tracked tree their own way.\n- **Rule** (the author's own): a shared fixture is the right move at four, not three — this node exists so the fourth sweep triggers it instead of becoming the fourth spelling.\n- **Also owed a human call**, recorded here rather than lost: docs/RCA/2026-08-11-roadmap-stamp-reverts.md:64 still names docs/roadmap.jsonl inside a dated, explicitly-unbuilt proposal — correct the path or let the dated document stand as written.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"177","pr":"227"}}
{"id":"pr-body-wrap","ord":"aU","title":"PR: repo markdown unwraps — one line per paragraph, 80 columns stays for source comments","done":"2026-08-15T14:47:49-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 from the human's root-cause exchange with a lane: agents hard-wrapped PR bodies at ~80 because the repo's own docs/*.md do — the habit inherits from the corpus.\n\n- **Fix** targets the SOURCE: unwrap the repo's markdown prose (README, docs/*.md, brainstorming, package READMEs) to one line per paragraph.\n  - Code blocks, tables, ASCII diagrams untouched, rendered output identical.\n  - Convention written in HACKING.md: markdown prose never hard-wraps; ~80 stays for source comments.\n- PR bodies themselves were explicitly scoped OUT (the human's correction mid-dispatch — the habit dies at the corpus, not by editing history).\n- **Now** (2026-08-15): Grok solo (terminal `3e7619c0`, branch `pr-bodies-unwrapped`), review WAIVED, fielded at green.\n  - A mid-dispatch scope correction was sent and acknowledged-by-conduct; the whitespace-shaped diff rebases trivially under whichever sibling lands second.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00"}
{"id":"quote-safe-selectors","ord":"aV","title":"PR: e2e steps should build their data- attribute selectors through one quote-safe helper #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:24-04:00","desc":"Filed at PR #182's close (2026-08-15), opencode's nit answered-not-fixed with the receipt on the record.\n\n- Solid sets dynamic attributes via setAttribute so the DOM is escaped by construction — this is a test-selector concern only.\n- data-from was the fourth instance of one house idiom (data-path, data-file, data-node-id).\n- Hardening only the newest made the suite inconsistent for zero coverage.\n- **Fix:** one quote-safe helper across every data- step in packages/tests/step_definitions/.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"182","pr":"227"}}
{"id":"html-memory","ord":"aW","title":"PR: .html bodies stop living whole in the set — big pages want lazy bodies or a cap","done":"2026-08-16T12:55:44-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #189 (2026-08-15).\n\n- Every .html body is held in the loaded set for the process lifetime (ops/codec.ts:44, format/set.ts:53).\n- Saved pages are megabytes with assets inlined — resident memory scales with vault content, no eviction, no cap.\n- Named in docs/format.md:122.\n- **Fix direction:** bodies loaded on read (the snapshot-scale precedent — documents already stopped riding the first frame once) or a size-gated claim that refuses in words.","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"204"}}
{"id":"siblings-of-quadratic","parent":"model-indices","ord":"Zz","title":"Slice 1: the index shape — byFile, mirrorsOf, edgesTo in Derived; every scan becomes a lookup #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T12:30:00-04:00","desc":"Ruled 2026-08-16: docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md commits to direction C — patch the in-memory view when a file changes instead of rebuilding it three times per edit (the emanote shape).\n\n- C lands in four shippable slices; this node is slice 1: give `Derived` real indexes.\n  - `byFile` (file → its nodes), killing every by-file scan: `siblingsOf`, `nodesOf`, the trash page, the per-candidate loops.\n  - Plus the reverse maps the later patcher needs: `mirrorsOf` (target → mirrors resolving to it); `edgesTo` (target → sources whose after/blocks edges land on it).\n  - Built in the same single pass as today's tables, with every scan site converted to index reads.\n  - Still full-rebuild-per-edit at this slice.\n- Slices 2–4 (one computation per edit; the patcher with its oracle property test; patches on the wire) become their own roadmap items when the human says dispatch.\n- **Library scan concluded:** hand-rolled Maps, no dependency — d2ts/TanStack DB are the ideas' productized form but the wrong bite.\n- Grok's #198 warning about a \"blind\" shared grouping helper is answered by putting the grouping inside `Derived`, always paired with its revision.","created":"2026-08-15T21:31:01-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"205"}}
{"id":"viewport-helper-promotion","ord":"aX","title":"viewport() joins OlaiWorld — nine step files spell it inline #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T09:17:25-04:00","desc":"Filed from PR #197's deferral (2026-08-15): the e2e world's own convention says a helper belongs on OlaiWorld once three or four features ask; nine step files spell viewport() inline. Converting them was six files outside #197's diff. Mechanical.","created":"2026-08-15T21:43:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"200"}}
{"id":"drawnorsaid-extra-frame","ord":"aY","title":"drawnOrSaid waits one extra frame on the happy path — grok's #199 follow-up #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T09:17:27-04:00","desc":"Filed from grok's #199 review (2026-08-16): the one follow-up it would take — an extra frame on drawnOrSaid's happy path so the pointer and the keys agree about when the tab has the way back. Small, e2e-harness precision.","created":"2026-08-15T23:47:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"200"}}
{"id":"model-indices","ord":"aZ","title":"Model indices: patch the view, don't rebuild it (direction C)","desc":"**Plan of record, ruled 2026-08-16:** docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md.\n- Four shippable slices, in order — each a PR with its own evidence.\n- **End state:**\n  - One small edit costs what it touched, not three whole-corpus rebuilds.\n  - The patcher speaks Surface's own collection-delta frame.\n  - from-scratch `derive()` stays as the oracle a property test holds the patcher to.","created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00"}
{"id":"model-indices-2","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a0","title":"Slice 2: compute the view once per edit — validate's Derived flows through to publish","done":"2026-08-16T15:51:51-04:00","desc":"Thread the validated view through to the publish step instead of recomputing it over the whole corpus (today's second rebuild). Old direction B, now C's plumbing. Open question 4 of the doc (serving derived facts through Surface's derived.collection reconciler) is a later refinement, not this slice.","after":["siblings-of-quadratic"],"created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T15:51:56-04:00","custom":{"pr":"208"}}
{"id":"model-indices-3","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a1","title":"Slice 3: the patcher — patch(derived, delta) in format/, held to the derive() oracle","done":"2026-08-17T08:45:18-04:00","desc":"One function beside `derive()` in format/, consuming Surface's collection-delta frame (`{upserts, removes}`).\n- Local updates: byFile, children keys owned by the file, byId with duplicate-claimant promotion.\n- A dirty set from the reverse indexes (mirrorsOf, edgesTo) recomputes only touched status/blocked entries.\n- Cycle checks re-run only when edges/mirrors changed.\n- **Copy-on-write:** a patch returns a NEW Derived, sharing untouched maps.\n- **Safety line:** the oracle property test — `patch(derive(before), delta)` deep-equals `derive(after)` over generated edit sequences, duplicate ids on purpose.\n  - The patcher may bail to full `derive()` on hairy cases.\n- Server uses it; the browser still rebuilds in this slice.","after":["model-indices-2"],"created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"211"}}
{"id":"model-indices-4","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a2","title":"Slice 4: the browser joins — the derived memo folds delta frames through the same patcher","done":"2026-08-17T12:06:05-04:00","desc":"- Swap `web/src/client/outlines.ts`'s derived memo from flatten-and-derive() to the patcher, over the delta frames the outlines collection already delivers.\n- **No wire change** — outlines-as-collection already paid that cost.\n- State the mixed per-entry revs contract explicitly in the patcher's contract (same as today, not new unsoundness).\n- If the generic fold-a-collection combinator proves itself olai-free here, offer it upstream to kolu Surface as a small PR (the precompress-upstream route) — a consequence of the design, not a prerequisite.","after":["model-indices-3"],"created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"223"}}
{"id":"check-targets-index","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a3","title":"checkTargets still walks per node — convert to the reverse index without moving error order #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T02:04:15-04:00","desc":"**Resolved 2026-08-17 overnight:** the conversion turned out already done by #208 (slice 2), held behind three pins two of which fail on the walk.\n- PR #218 records it in model-indices.md with the measurement: walk 4.0ms vs index 0.40ms clean; 144ms vs 3.8ms with 200 unknown namings.\n  - didYouMean per-unknown-id (25 calls vs 200) is the larger factor.\n- **Honest close:** done by #208, measured by #218.","created":"2026-08-16T12:17:29-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"205","pr":"218"}}
{"id":"watch-set-per-connection","ord":"aa","title":"Bodies stay live by refcount, not a 16-slot guess — the wire learns when a reader leaves #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T20:41:08-04:00","desc":"**Reframed 2026-08-17** after reviewing kolu's watchers (was: \"per-connection LRU?\", #204's deferrals 3–5).\n- The 16-path set in `packages/server/src/bodies.ts` is not file-watching (the store already watches the whole directory) — it decides which OPEN pages get their bodies re-read when a revision touches them.\n- The bound exists only because the wire says when a reader OPENS a key and never says when the last one LEAVES (\"the framework owns subscription lifetime and does not publish it\" — bodies.ts).\n  - So eviction is a guess aged out of an LRU, and sixteen newer opens anywhere silence a still-visible page (stale, never wrong; reopen heals; documented in docs/format.md).\n\n**Kolu's honest shape** (`packages/integrations/io/src/refcounted-dir-watcher.ts`, `packages/integrations/git/src/working-tree-watcher.ts`): refcounted subscription per key.\n- First subscribe installs, every consumer shares, last unsubscribe tears down.\n- No cap, no LRU, no per-connection question, because the leave signal EXISTS.\n\n**The fix:**\n- Expose subscription lifetime on olai's wire (the \"keys-style member for who holds this key\" bodies.ts names as its own replacement), and refcount bodies on it — live for exactly the pages somebody has open, no magic number anywhere.\n- Both documented format.md edges (the silenced page; the birth-announce gap in published.ts) get revisited by the same change.\n- **Superseded:** the original per-connection-LRU idea — it would shrink the blast radius while keeping the guess.","created":"2026-08-16T12:49:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"204","pr":"229"}}
{"id":"kolu-create-placement","ord":"ab","title":"Upstream: kolu's create-terminal endpoint should demand explicit placement — toplevel or child-of #upstream","done":"2026-08-16T21:20:12-04:00","desc":"**Proposed by the human 2026-08-16**, after the orchestrator drifted into spawning reviewers as top-level terminals when the charter said splits — the default absorbed the mistake silently, and the canvas's hierarchy (who works for whom) quietly flattened.\n\n**The design**, simplified on the human's challenge (\"what interactive CLI?\"): humans create terminals through the kolu web canvas, not the CLI — the CLI's real audience is scripts and agents, exactly the callers that drift.\n- No TTY carve-out, no default anywhere.\n- The padi create endpoint takes a REQUIRED placement — `toplevel | childOf(terminalId)`.\n- The CLI requires exactly one of `--toplevel` or `--parent <id>`, erroring otherwise.\n\n**Scope added by the human same day:** the rule also covers kolu's MCP surface.\n- The create-terminal tool `kolu mcp` offers agents takes the same required placement with no default, refusing a call that omits it — agents over MCP are exactly the script-shaped callers the rule exists for.\n- Migration is one word per script.\n\nA kolu PR, dispatched (lane `kolu-create-placement`).","created":"2026-08-16T14:15:53-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"2173"}}
{"id":"kolu-watch-next-cli","ord":"ac","title":"Upstream: the ring — padi nags every settled terminal by default until it is worked, snoozed with a reason, or killed #upstream","done":"2026-08-19T10:57:20-04:00","desc":"**Rev 3** of docs/brainstorming/kolu-watch-cli.md — simplified on the human's ruling (rev 2's five-command watchdog was too much; we own both tools, no compat debt).\n\n**The whole design:**\n- **The ring**, default padi behavior — a terminal settled ≥60s is *ringing*, level-triggered, cleared only by work/death/snooze, so missed wakeups are structurally impossible.\n- **One verb:** `kolu snooze <id> --for 2h --reason \"…\"` — the only way to legitimize idleness, reason+expiry mandatory, expiry re-rings.\n- **One face:** `kolu ring --wait` — block until any terminal rings, print, exit; its exit is the orchestrator's wake.\n- Same state via the urgency resource for MCP (lingerIds already half-exists).\n\n**Deletes rev 2's:** subscriptions, ack cursors, expect/park, `--settled-ms`, screenTail-in-events — all of it was delivery machinery for a problem level-triggering doesn't have.","created":"2026-08-16T17:18:14-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"kolu #2181 merged by the human 2026-08-18; dogfooded live (snapshot/transition/nag all observed)"}}
{"id":"kolu-darwin-unit-fsevents","ord":"ad","title":"Upstream: darwin's unit lane is structurally red (git FSEvents churn tests), which silently skips every darwin daemon suite and blocks merges #upstream","done":"2026-08-17T00:40:26-04:00","desc":"**Surfaced by #2173's author and ruled DISPATCH by the human 2026-08-16.** Two coupled facts:\n- `ci::unit@aarch64-darwin` has 20+ consecutive reds on ci@petit from the git FSEvents churn tests (packages/integrations/), reproducing byte-identically on unmodified master.\n- `ci/mod.just` declares `daemon: install unit`, so while unit is red on darwin the daemon suites there are SKIPPED — darwin daemon coverage is not exercised at all, and the red required context forced #2173 to merge via `--admin`.\n- **Fix:** the churn tests for real if the failure mode allows (preferred), or skip them properly on darwin with the reasoning pinned — note PR #2172's branch already skips two of them darwin-only, so reconcile rather than collide.\n- **Success** = darwin unit green on master, daemon suites running on darwin again.","created":"2026-08-16T21:21:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"2176"}}
{"id":"patch-bench-harness","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a5","title":"Commit the 1,000-file patch-vs-rebuild benchmark as a just leg so the order-of-magnitude figure is reproducible #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T22:38:02-04:00","desc":"Open question 5 of docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md.\n- The slice-3 author measured 2–3ms patched vs 25–40ms rebuilt on a 1,000-file / 21,000-record vault as a one-off.\n- The harness is not in the tree, so README/architecture.md deliberately call it an unreproducible laptop sample.\n- **Fix:** commit the harness with a `just` leg.\n- From PR #211; filed on the human's overnight draft ruling.","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:17-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"211"}}
{"id":"patch-byid-overlay","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a6","title":"Replace the patcher's new Map(byId) clone — roughly half of every patch — with an overlay or persistent map #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T22:38:02-04:00","desc":"Open question 1 of docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md, now answered with a measurement by the slice-3 author: the byId clone is the dominant remaining cost (~half a patch). The lever is an overlay map or a persistent structure — take it when a bigger vault asks. From PR #211; filed on the human's overnight draft ruling.","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-17T22:38:02-04:00","custom":{"from":"211"}}
{"id":"second-pane","ord":"ae","title":"The Second Pane — split views: N panes, each a full page, the layout in the URL","done":"2026-08-17T17:56:34-04:00","desc":"Proposed in the artifact \"The Second Pane\" (claude.ai/code/artifact/980a4438-9c7f-4e1b-b5b7-18a647c6b379), researched against Workflowy's native panes and the MultiFlow extension.\n\n**Principles:**\n- A pane is a route (page + zoom + filter) rendering the full page component — no second-class panes.\n- Focus is explicit with a visible ring and all shortcuts/palette/filter acting on it.\n- Links deterministic (click = this pane, mod-click = open right).\n- The whole layout serializes into the URL (share/restore/back-forward).\n- Drag between panes native (one store, no frames).\n- Saved layouts are outline nodes.\n\nDispatched to grok 2026-08-17 on the human's word — draft PR, NO agent reviewers, the human reviews by running the branch.","created":"2026-08-17T10:39:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"225"}}
{"id":"olai-batch-verbs","ord":"af","title":"MCP writes stop costing one round-trip per fact — add_node children carry the whole record, a batch apply runs many ops in one atomic write, and update writes several fields of one node","done":"2026-08-17T12:39:00-04:00","desc":"From the 2026-08-17 orchestration retrospective: a lane spawn cost ~13 olai MCP calls (1 add_node + 9 set_after + 3 set_prop) because each fact is its own round-trip — and the agent's turn latency, not the server, is the cost.\n\n**One PR, three verbs:**\n- `add_node`'s child shape gains `after`, `see`, and `props` so a captured subtree arrives with its edges and facts in the same atomic write.\n- `apply` — a list of ops executed in order, one validation, one write, one rev, all-or-nothing with the failing op named.\n- `update {id, mark?, desc?, props?, after?}` for the done+sha+note trio.\n\n- Every refusal the single verbs make (shadowed keys, unknown ids with closest match, cycles named, done-over-unfinished from #207), the batch forms must make identically.\n- **Ruled:** auto-merge on clean evidence.","created":"2026-08-17T10:44:55-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"224"}}
{"id":"kolu-one-shot-submit","ord":"ag","title":"Upstream: one-shot dispatch to an agent terminal #upstream","todo":true,"desc":"**The claim:** dispatching a message to an agent terminal becomes ONE call — `sendInput` grows a `submit` option, and `create` grows a `message` option.\n\n**PR #2177 CLOSED UNMERGED by the human's ruling 2026-08-18** after three rounds of live field testing (full reason on the PR): the core premise — output-quiet means prompt-ready — is false in the field.\n- Round 1 lost a brief to a boot race.\n- Round 2's recognition fix was circular (recognition is downstream of the first message).\n- Round 3 fixed claude via foreground-process identity, but grok still starved both one-shot paths — its idle TUI repaints on a ~0.8–1.5s cadence, so the 1500ms default settle never holds (settleMs:800 submits instantly; the manual trio works).\n\n**Post-mortem for the successor:**\n- Keep the mid-turn refusal semantics, the 30s wire-pinned bound, the readiness-proof structure, and the commandName/adapter recognition work (branch `one-shot-submit` preserved).\n- Replace the quiet-conjunct with a signal that is agent-state-shaped — the adapter already knows idle; padi should ask it, not the byte stream.\n- **Related:** `kolu-watch-next-cli` (PR #2181 in flight) encodes the same lesson for supervision.","created":"2026-08-17T10:44:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00"}
{"id":"faithful-addresses","ord":"ah","title":"The address system is not faithful to the directory #needs-brainstorm #human","todo":true,"desc":"Raised by the human 2026-08-17 while designing saved layouts, and parked for its own brainstorm before any dispatch.\n\n**The complaint:** `/o/notes.olai` and `/doc/docs/x.md` invent structure the disk does not have — the file lives at `notes.olai`, so the address should be `/notes.olai`.\n- routes.ts convicts itself: it refuses a `/html/` prefix on the grounds that \"the suffix is what fileKind reads, and it is in the address either way\" — a prefix would be \"the same fact spelled twice, free to disagree with the name it carries\".\n- But `/o/` vs `/doc/` is that same duplication, since `.olai` vs `.md` already says which kind of page it is.\n\n**The human's sketch:** file paths ARE the addresses (`/notes.olai`), and special/computed pages wear a marker that cannot collide with a filename — something like `/:today`, `/:agenda`, `/:trash`.\n- Wanted done properly, as a SYSTEM, from the hickey/lowy standpoint rather than patched address by address.\n- **Hickey:** is the address complecting \"which file\" with \"which kind of page\" and \"which view of it\"?\n- **Lowy:** what volatility does the address layer encapsulate, and would its interface survive the axis it claims to own changing (new page kinds, new view parameters, nesting)?\n\n**Two obstacles a design must answer explicitly:**\n- **Collision:** once file paths sit at the root, a file named `agenda` collides with the view. Hence the human's `:` marker (or another reserved shape) — decide it, don't leave it implicit.\n- **The node permalink:** `/n/<id>` deliberately spells ONLY an id, because ids survive renames and moves across files; a faithful `/notes.olai?id=hinge-notes` re-introduces a file that can disagree with reality after a move.\n  - Either the file is a hint the resolver repairs, or the id stays canonical with the path decorative, or something better. This is the real tension, not a detail.\n\n**Downstream:** saved layouts (and anything else that stores a route) must not be built until this is settled, or they bake in the current spelling.\n- Also: #225 landed the pane-list address (the workspace URL) on top of the current scheme, so a change here touches that bijection and its tests.","created":"2026-08-17T18:02:56-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-at-nodes","ord":"ai","title":"Chat: typing @ completes NODES too, not just file paths — hand the agent a task by name","done":"2026-08-17T21:09:49-04:00","desc":"Chosen by the human 2026-08-17 as the next feature.\n- PR #213 gave the chat composer @-completion over FILE paths (server's own prune + kind registry, WeakMap fold, eight rows, tagOpensAt reused so @person habit does not collide).\n- **This is the other half:** the same @ also completes NODES — type `@hinge` and pick the node, so you can say \"look at @pick the hinges\" instead of pasting a path and hoping the agent finds the row.\n- Reuses the completion machinery just built rather than inventing a second one.","created":"2026-08-17T18:05:22-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"pr":"228"}}
{"id":"mentions-index-one-sigil","ord":"aj","title":"The mention index files only @ — one taggedBy would also free the tag completion from walking the corpus #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-18T21:55:00-04:00","desc":"Filed at PR #237 by the altitude pass; SHIPPED in PR #249.\n\n- **Problem:** mentionedBy filed the @ namespace and dropped the sigil, but the fold it rode (titleParts) already yielded #topic parts and threw them away — so the index was HALF a reverse index of tags written in prose.\n- **Fix:** one taggedBy keyed by the WRITTEN form (@herbs and #herbs are two keys), re-keyed in one change across derive.ts, patch.ts's taggings(), the oracle's readable() and backlinksOf; mayHoldSigil went with it.\n- web/src/client/complete/tags.ts now reads the index instead of scanning every node of the corpus per derivation.\n- **Measured** (the deferral's condition): two new `just bench` legs print both halves.\n  - Completion: 18.5ms walked vs 0.47ms read (12.2ms for the title-only walk that was already there, answering 60 tags against the index's 1,052).\n  - Corpus-wide fold: 6.5ms filing @ alone vs 18.6ms filing both sigils.\n  - End to end, interleaved across two worktrees: a rebuild goes 32.8ms → 46.7ms, a one-file patch 0.67ms → 0.85ms, against ~18ms saved on every derivation while a tag is being typed.\n- **Verdict:** yes, with the cost stated — the saving is per keystroke, the cost is per cold rebuild.\n- **Bonus:** WIDENED the completion — a tag written in a note is now offered, and the count is one vote per record rather than per occurrence.","created":"2026-08-18T06:05:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"237"}}
{"id":"olai-convention-dir","ord":"ak","title":"_olai/Trash.olai is the one trash — the archive name dies; Inbox.olai stays top-level","done":"2026-08-19T21:52:16-04:00","desc":"Ruled with #246: minted convention files land in `_olai/` (underscore, not dot — the store prunes dot-directories); `Pins.olai` already mints there.\n\n- **CORRECTED AND EXTENDED by the human 2026-08-19** (supersedes the earlier \"Archive.olai and Inbox.olai follow Pins.olai\" spelling):\n\n1. **There is ONE trash: `_olai/Trash.olai`.**\n   - The per-directory Archive.olai convention dies.\n   - Trashing a node from any outline writes into that one file (an entry must therefore record which outline it came from, so untrashing can put it back).\n2. **Inbox.olai stays top-level** — it does not move into `_olai/`; its by-name resolution and root minting are untouched.\n3. **Full rename, the human's word**: the file, the verbs and the operator all say trash.\n   - `archive_node`/`unarchive_node` become `trash_node`/`untrash_node`; `empty_trash` empties `_olai/Trash.olai`; `is:archived` becomes `is:trashed`.\n   - \"archive\" as a word leaves the product (tools, search grammar, web faces, docs).\n   - BREAKING for agents; blessed.\n4. **Existing per-directory Archive.olai files are left on disk and STOP being read**: no longer trash, not drawn on the trash page, invisible to `is:trashed` — orphaned until a human hand-moves them.\n   - No migration in this PR.\n\n- **Docs to sweep:** format.md, architecture.md wherever Archive.olai is named, the MCP face/charter text, search grammar docs.\n- **Dispatch shape:** Grok authors, opencode is the single review seat, and the debate happens as PR-comment back-and-forth until both settle (the human's ruling on all three points, 2026-08-19).","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"#246 (the human's ruling 2026-08-19)","pr":"#266 merged 3f70317c"}}
{"id":"dev-server-random-port","ord":"al","title":"A dev server never squats the production port — port 0 by default, fixed ports are a deploy's explicit word","done":"2026-08-19T19:28:23-04:00","desc":"Two field incidents in one night, same defect class.\n\n- **(1)** a dev instance bound `127.0.0.1:7714` — the production port — so the orchestrator's olai MCP answered with the dev vault's outlines all evening and the ledger was wrongly believed unreachable.\n- **(2)** the empty-trash lane's e2e dialed ANOTHER worktree's server through the shared `/tmp/olai-dev` convention and failed against a foreign bundle.\n- **Fix:** dev and e2e servers bind port 0 (OS-assigned), print the port at startup and write it to a per-worktree file the harness reads back; a fixed `--port` is something only a deploy passes explicitly.\n- Then a dev instance cannot squat production and two worktrees cannot dial each other.","created":"2026-08-19T11:02:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"2026-08-19 incident (the human's diagnosis)","pr":"#264 merged 82b1c543"}}
{"id":"private-dir-export","ord":"am","title":"isPrivateOwnedDir exports from kolu; olai deletes its copy — debate #3 finding 3, both-side PRs","done":"2026-08-19T16:55:36-04:00","desc":"Dispatched 2026-08-19 on the human's word while they read the debate conclusion (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md, finding 3).\n\n- **Two PRs by one Grok lane:**\n  - **(1) kolu** — export the `isPrivateOwnedDir` predicate from `@kolu/surface`'s unix-socket module.\n  - **(2) olai** — bump the kolu pin and delete `notPrivatelyOurs` (packages/server/src/lock.ts:318-334, which carries its own death-note: \"if upstream ever exports it, this function is the thing to delete\").\n- Signed by all three debaters across three rounds; sized as a fix, not a vault.","created":"2026-08-19T13:49:45-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"agent":"grok","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 3","kolu-pr":"#2186 merged 1b3c20b5 (approved by the human 2026-08-19); olai-side PR B in flight","olai-pr":"#259 merged 0f551b2f — merged by the pipeline's own law (dag-pr-deferrals: a no-deferrals report skips the human gate), after the orchestrator wrongly parked it on an invented approval; both reviews do-not-object, CI green at a1d29c02. Finding 3 closed whole.","terminal":"0b26abe6-7c68-428a-ac42-d1a91019f734"}}
{"id":"surface-deltas-frame","ord":"an","title":"The deltas frame is the unit of update — kolu hands \"what changed\" through; deriving.ts dies #upstream","done":"2026-08-19T18:12:02-04:00","desc":"Debate #3's headline (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md finding 1), ratified by the human 2026-08-19.\n\n- **Change:** ONE socket in `@kolu/surface`'s client half, two faces shipping together.\n  - The named-key in-place merge (no whole-dict copy, no N-walk — the measured biggest cost of typing into a big vault).\n  - The `fold({init, step})` member on deltas-verb handles, type-gated.\n- **Amendment from the kolu-benefit survey:** export `useCollectionDeltas` from the solid barrel.\n- `rev` stays (wire contract); `@olai/format`'s patch stays.\n- **Spec** with signatures, semantics and edge cases: docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md §Finding 1.\n- **Beneficiaries proven:**\n  - olai deletes `deriving.ts` whole (`outlines.ts` hands frames straight to patch).\n  - drishti deletes its hand-rolled `foldProcessDeltas` (the drishti pair-PR is the adoption vehicle, not a re-green).\n  - Four more drishti collections stop paying the silent copy.\n- **Ships** as a kolu PR under the drishti pair-PR gate + odu-impact check (additive; expected verdict adoption-opportunity, to be confirmed by the mandated grep), then olai bumps the pin and the deletion is the installation.","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus, terminal f08e17da-421c-47bc-8ff1-05146cda854a, kolu worktree surface-deltas-frame (one lane, two PRs, drishti+odu along the way — dispatched 2026-08-19)","drishti":"#143 merged 185efde4 — foldProcessDeltas deleted, the process table adopts the exported hook; olai's deletion PR in flight (lane vaults-installed)","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 1","kolu-pr":"#2187 merged b4694c28 (approved by the human; both reviews do-not-object; --admin merge since kolu's base policy refuses self-approval). Remaining: drishti #143 re-pin + merge, then olai deletes deriving.ts at the pin bump","olai-pr":"#263 merged b33fea13 (approved by the human, pipeline waived for the deletion shape) — deriving.ts died whole; kolu's own e2e bench carries the kill: up to 937× by frame shape; deferrals filed as vaults-installed-deferrals","spec":"docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md"}}
{"id":"surface-holders","ord":"ao","title":"CollectionHandlerDeps.holders — the framework says when the last reader leaves; holding.ts dies #upstream","done":"2026-08-19T18:12:03-04:00","desc":"Debate #3 finding 2 (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md), ratified by the human 2026-08-19.\n\n- **Change:** one OPTIONAL member on kolu's `CollectionHandlerDeps`: `holders?: (key) => Effect<unknown, never, Scope>`.\n  - Run via `Stream.unwrap` in the per-reader get stream's own scope, BEFORE `readOne` (the pull order is contract; `holding.ts`'s test moves upstream as the framework's pin).\n  - Scope close is the release; never error channel (a defect crashes that subscription loudly, no unheld degrade).\n  - Absent → byte-identical path.\n- **Spec:** docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md §Finding 2.\n- **Grenade already went off here:** the #229 sixteen-path LRU.\n- olai deletes `holding.ts` + its test whole; `runtime.ts` says `holders: bodies.held`; `bodies.ts` stays entirely; the client-side askers map stays out (separate axis, ruled).\n- odu's logs store is a proven second consumer (adoption-opportunity on its ledger at next bump).\n- Same shipping gates as surface-deltas-frame; ranked under it by the debate (younger plug, one consumer).","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:26-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"agent":"same lane as surface-deltas-frame (terminal f08e17da) — second PR from a second branch after the first opens","drishti":"#144 closed as a no-op — #143 landed first carrying the same pin; nothing to adopt (drishti impact was nil, as the review proved by grep)","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 2","kolu-pr":"#2188 merged f648f0a2 (approved by the human; both reviews do-not-object; one conflict round after #2187 landed, resolved by master merge at 59cc7dcd). Remaining: drishti #144 merge, then olai deletes holding.ts at the pin bump","olai-pr":"#263 merged b33fea13 — holding.ts and its test died whole; runtime.ts says holders: bodies.held; the pull-order pin verified living upstream before deletion","spec":"docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md"}}
{"id":"debate3-claim-tests","ord":"ap","title":"Three claim tests from debate #3 — promises pinned as tests, not comments","todo":true,"desc":"Ratified 2026-08-19 (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md finding 4). One small PR.\n\n- **(a)** address recognition has one door — `addressIn` delegates to `routeIn`, no module outside `routes.ts` implements recognition, the bijection comparison belongs to `routes.test.ts`.\n  - Was meant to ride the fcd-addresses PR; #256 merged without it, so it lands here — or rides fcd-pr2-face if that diff touches routes anyway.\n- **(b)** `createArrival` call sites keep literal `import()` specifiers (the bundler reads them statically).\n  - Today the rule is a comment at arriving.ts:38-42; the third chunk, ink-mde, is already on the roadmap.\n- **(c) interim** — nothing outside `holding.ts`, its test, and `runtime.ts` spells the get-tag wrap / `Stream.unwrap` hold; this one dies with surface-holders and should say so in its test name.\n- The debate caught two records rotting mid-sitting (the package-survey sentence and the roadmap's store stillness stamp) — that is the argument for these, demonstrated on the debate's own inputs.","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:35-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 4"}}
{"id":"web-testlib-face","ord":"aq","title":"@olai/web gains a ./testlib face","todo":true,"desc":"Ratified 2026-08-19 (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md finding 5) — boundary hygiene, explicitly NOT counted as a receptacle.\n\n- **Problem:** `packages/tests` imports sixteen distinct `@olai/web/src/client/…` files by package name into `src/`, under a manifest that declares `\"exports\": \"None.\"` — both statements cannot be true.\n- **Fix:** a narrow published test-face (`./testlib`, the convention format/git/log/ops already carry) covering the handles the suite actually needs.\n  - The manifest sentence is rewritten in the same diff — a socket must not be installed against a header that still denies it exists.\n- The one-line `./testids` export was proposed and killed in-debate (a bandage leaving fifteen doors wireless).\n- The room recorded the honest alternatives (rewrite the comment to name reality, or tests stop reaching src) if the human prefers either.","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:43-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 5"}}
{"id":"e2e-earn-browser","ord":"ar","title":"The e2e suite sheds what a browser doesn't earn — ~150 of 875 scenarios cut on the audit","done":"2026-08-19T22:34:25-04:00","desc":"The human's principle, distilled: an e2e scenario must EARN the browser.\n- Cut categories from the audit: (a) ~67 unit-test-shaped (a unit test already pins the law — filter grammar ×15, move_to_picker ×7, an_external_agent ×14…); (b) ~36 trivial/static render assertions; (c) ~34 one-law-many-doors permutations (keep one representative door); (d) ~14 pixel/geometry pins; (e) a few obsolete (the connection scenarios the offline-overlay ruling replaces are left for THAT PR to rewrite).\n- Every cut must verify its claimed unit-test overlap first; an unpinned claim gets its unit test in the same commit, never a bare delete.\n- The PR also writes the principle into packages/tests/README.md so it binds future authors, and records e2e wall time before/after.\n- KEEP class (earns the browser): stacking via elementFromPoint, real drag/touch, live-wire (watcher edits, reconnects, server death), multi-tab races, CSP/iframe sealing.","created":"2026-08-19T20:50:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"agent":"grok","from":"the human 2026-08-19 (audit commissioned in chat; dispatch + merge pre-approved)","pr":"#269 merged c7806133; suite 875→717 scenarios, e2e ~3m32s→~3m7s; principle written into packages/tests/README.md"}}
{"id":"olai-service-sigterm","ord":"as","title":"olai.service dies by outside SIGTERM after hours up — twice in one night, the ledger goes dark each time","done":"2026-08-20T10:34:15-04:00","desc":"Observed twice while the service ran the pinned binary /nix/store/ylxg…-olai:\n- 23:06 EDT: exit 130 after 2h17m up (journal: received SIGTERM); ledger dark 105 min until the orchestrator restarted it.\n- 06:01 EDT: exit 130 after 5h09m up (journal: received SIGTERM); restarted within the hour.\n- **Mechanism (corrected 2026-08-20 from the live unit):** the unit DID carry `Restart=on-failure` — beside `SuccessExitStatus=130`, which declares the SIGTERM exit a success, so on-failure never fired. At both deaths the journal shows `received SIGTERM` with NO systemd `Stopping`/`Stopped` (the deliberate 20:49 / 08:12 restarts log `Stopped`): something signalled the process directly, in nix-daemon-heavy windows while overnight lanes ran e2e/CI.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #280 (Grok, merged aef63ec76):** `Restart=always` + `RestartSec=1s`, `SuccessExitStatus=130` kept (systemd never restarts a `systemctl stop`, so deliberate stops stay deliberate; a stray SIGTERM now costs ~1s). Proven on transient units without touching the live service; check.nix asserts it; running.md describes it; RCA at docs/RCA/2026-08-20-olai-service-sigterm.md. Darwin already restarted a 130 (`SuccessfulExit=false`).\n- **Sender: unknown.** Every kill path in this repo and in the odu/kolu tooling was read and ruled out in the RCA's table (the e2e harness SIGKILLs its own child; wire/evidence scripts kill `$!`; `just serve` kills its own group; kolu dev-clean checks a state-root manifest; nix builds are PID-namespaced). If it recurs, the unit comes back and the journal's `received SIGTERM` without `Stopped` still names an outside signal.\n- **Third death, 11:54:18 EDT, before the deploy:** same shape (received SIGTERM, `Consumed … over 3h 42min`, no Stopping/Stopped, exit 130 = success, NRestarts=0) under the still-old unit started 08:12. Timing note for the sender hunt: within a minute of the orchestrator spawning reactivity PR 3's Kolu terminal and its Claude Code session booting (11:53–11:54); the earlier two also fell in lane-spawn/CI windows. Ledger dark 4 min — the human deployed at 11:58.\n- **Deployed 2026-08-20 11:58** (home-manager switch by the human): the live unit now reads Restart=always / RestartSec=1s / SuccessExitStatus=130 on /nix/store/i2v7hgc1…-olai. The next outside SIGTERM is the proof; `NRestarts` will say.","created":"2026-08-20T06:51:51-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"the orchestrator's overnight observations 2026-08-19→20"}}
{"id":"archive-migrate-vault","ord":"at","title":"Migrate this vault's two leftover Archive.olai files into _olai/Trash.olai — the one trash holds what the archives held","done":"2026-08-20T13:46:02-04:00","desc":"The human's ask, 2026-08-20 13:08: \"did we migrate the old file to new file path? if not do it.\" #266 (olai-convention-dir) shipped the one trash with the 2026-08-19 ruling \"leave-and-stop-reading, no migration\" — so `docs/Archive.olai` (25 records) and `docs/orchestrator/Archive.olai` (13) were still on disk, dormant. Root cause of there being TWO: the pre-#266 rule put an archive \"beside the outline it left\", one per directory — the orchestrator's 2026-08-19 put-away of the What's-new lane from `orchestrator/lanes.olai` minted the second.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #291 (Grok, merged afa76be11; review waived by the human).** One `_olai/Trash.olai` of 40 records: outermost signposts `roadmap.olai` and `orchestrator/lanes.olai`, then the archives' ancestor-title chains, then the records untouched (git sees a rename of docs/Archive.olai plus the 13 appended). Both Archive.olai files gone. Proven through the product's faces on a copy: validator ok (49 files), trash page draws both groups, `is:trashed` 40/40, default search misses them, `untrash_node` resolves a sample from each group by the recorded chain without overrides. The migration script ran once and was not shipped; format.md's leftover-archive rule is unchanged.\n- **Open question for the human (from the PR body):** should the PRODUCT offer this wrapping to every vault that still holds leftover `Archive.olai` files? Not built here.","created":"2026-08-20T13:08:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:33:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-20","merge":"on the human's 'do it'"}}
